rchase doesn't seem to have  been a huge risk for the streaming giant  given that the acquisition happened in  2017 what took so long for the series to  end up on netflix  miller told the hollywood reporter in  april 2021 that he had spent time  focusing more on the series quality  rather than worrying about how quickly  he could get it out saying you can do it  fast or you can do it brilliant  that's my philosophy still heeding stan  lee's advice miller made sure that he  would remain president of miller world  even after the acquisition  in a may 2021 press release about  jupiter's legacy miller noted when my  wife lucy and i sold miller world to  netflix in 2017  our first priority was jupiter's legacy  we had flirted with the idea of a movie  but netflix supported us the chance to  make this adaptation as big and deep as  it needed to be  miller first conceptualized the  jupiter's legacy series in 2008 but the  first issue wasn't published until 2013.  miller handled the words while frank  quietly handled the series illustrations  and pete doherty took on the lettering  as miller told the hollywood reporter  the jupiter's legacy comics are the  longest running series miller has ever  published  spanning over 20 issues the netflix  series covers five issues over a single  eight episode season compared to comic  book universes like dc and marvel eight  years between publishing the first comic  and landing a massive netflix deal for  the series isn't exactly a long wait  time  some comics take decades to get adapted  for the screen so going from the page to  a full-scale film production in that  short a time is far from ordinary of  course it helps that jupiter's legacy is  far from mark miller's first foray into  hollywood  with his resume it was only a matter of  time before jupiter's legacy was added  to his filmography  few directors have had more success with  superhero movies than james gunn  the director brought guardians of the  galaxy to the big screen for the first  time establishing a new beloved  franchise in the marvel film canon he  also picked up the pieces from dc's  suicide squad property with a reimagined  follow-up  2021's a suicide squad so when gunn gave  miller advised about what he should do  with his jupiter's legacy property  miller had good reason to listen while  jupiter's legacy was initially conceived  as a trilogy film series in 2015 with  lorenzo d  bonaventura in a production role miller  discarded the plan with a push from gun  during an interview with denim geek mark  miller revealed that gunn told him that  the comics could never work as a movie  much of miller's success comes from  listening to those who have come before  him and he proved more than willing to  listen to this advice  as miller told den of geek quote the  smartest guy in the world is james gunn  most tv shows with heavy backstory take  an episode or two to lay out the origin  story when delving into the character's  histories but mark miller had other  ideas with jupiter's legacy  instead of spending a minute or 40  delving into the history of the first  superheroes and the jupiter's legacy  canon we get to watch the historical  origins of the union of justice members  be revealed throughout the series one  piece at a time  jumping between past and present the  series dips into its character's great  depression backstory covering their  respective histories when it's relevant  to do so  so what exactly influenced miller to  take this route during an interview with  the rap he revealed that the godfather  part 2 provided the inspiration for the  series woven time jumps  according to miller the idea was pitched  by stephen denying the original  showrunner for jupiter's legacy in the  same way that michael corleone and his  father vito's stories play out at the  same time  decades apart so tooed to the stories of  sheldon and brandon in jupiter's legacy  miller explained the godfather 2  structure shows the father and the son  at the same age  and that's the same thing that's being  done here to show the young characters  and the old characters at the same age  and essentially making the same mistakes  jupiter's legacy has an infinite number  of comic book parallels however the  deepest connection that skyfox actor  matt lanter sees might not be what you'd  expect the actor noted the similarities  between his jupiter's legacy character  and his role as anakin skywalker on star  wars the clone wars  and the outdated rules of conduct that  plagued the heroes of both worlds  lanter chatted with looper during an  exclusive interview where he compared  the rigid nature of the jedi council to  the strict rules of the union and  jupiter's legacy he said the jedi  council seems antiquated and just  doesn't apply in every situation anymore  and the jedi council is so black and  white in its thinking i think anakin  realized that things aren't black and  white  in fact there are shades of grey and  that's exactly what's going on in  jupiter's legacy  in both cases these unwavering rules  lead to the downfall of an otherwise  relatively moral hero the fickle beast  that is mother nature is something that  almost  every series or movie deals with at some  point during shooting when the weather  decides to do something unexpected  production has two options  roll with it or halt production luckily  for jupiter's legacy when the sky's open  for a dramatic snowstorm the weather  only enhanced the scene's otherworldly  quality  during an exclusive interview with  looper cinematographer nicole persh  whitaker  director of photography for several  episodes of jupiter's legacy  revealed the perils of filming in an  unpredictable canadian climate  in one episode in particular the series  is seventh the weather wasn't  cooperating  leading to heavy and unscripted snowfall  while they were shooting a scene in the  woods over the course of a few days  whitaker explained we all went back to  our hotels and woke up in the morning  and there was two feet of snow on the  ground which is very canadian  we were like oh my gosh there's a  snowstorm so basically we got the set  everybody talked about it and decided  this is an island that's alive so let's  embrace it so they started writing and  within an hour we had a new script  luckily for fans a surprise snow lends  an incredibly realistic backdrop to the  scene given that the characters head to  the island to claim their superpowers  they deal with a whole host of  challenges  now including unpredictable weather the  first flashback we get in jupiter's  legacy kicks off the events of the great  depression as the stock market crashes  while it's undoubtedly a fascinating  point in american history it's a unique  time period to place the origin story of  a group of slowly aging superheroes  however the period makes sense given the  year in which miller began writing the  comics  2008 marked a steady economic decline  leading to a financial crisis the likes  of which the world hadn't seen since a  great depression  the death of capitalism that is one hell  of a headline  miller told the hollywood reporter in  april 2021 when i sat down to do this it  was three years before i actually wrote  it during the financial crash in 2008.  i said i'm not going to do this unless i  can make it the greatest superhero story  of all time  setting the superhero's origin stories  in the late 20s with great depression  ties certainly set the story apart from  many of its counterparts  the choice roots the series in a reality  that almost everyone can relate to and  offers a unique vantage point for the  story to cover  as we've seen with the marvel cinematic  universe and dc extended universe  there's no shortage of stories waiting  to be told when film studios decide to  tap into comics characters legacies  with plenty of source material waiting  to be mined jupiter's legacy seemed  poised to enjoy a multiple season run on  netflix but any hopes fans may have had  for follow-up installments were dashed  in early june of 2021 when miller  announced that the cast had been  released from its contracts  although miller indicated that he hadn't  quite given up hope for more jupiter's  legacy on screen at some point in the  short term netflix's decision means the  show has been cancelled  on the bright side this frees miller up  for other projects like the upcoming  supercrook series he's set to debut for  the platform  it's still a bitter pill to swallow for  viewers who came to love the jupiter's  legacy characters throughout the show  but they can always turn to the comics  for more stories the latest chapter of  the saga jupiter's legacy requiem was  already set to begin arriving in comic  shops when the show's cancellation was  announced  so where exactly does miller world and  more specifically jupiter's legacy fall  in the comic book landscape  if you ask matt lanter he'll tell you  that it's the future of comics and  deserves a spot at the top with dc and  marvel  in fact we did ask matt lanter during a  looper exclusive interview  he said i think five years from now  everyone's going to know that it's  miller world it's dc  and it's marvel so i'll get to know  these characters now be the first on the  train and have fun with it man  that's a pretty big claim but it's not  without merit even though the series  isn't moving  forward on netflix the show still made a  huge impression on viewers with a rock  solid debut on the streamer coming in as  the number one program on the platform  upon its release  additionally as far as box office is  concerned miller's 2010 film kick-ass  brought in over 96 million dollars  worldwide and kingsmen the secret  service raked in over 414 million  dollars  those are numbers that are in the range  of or even surpassed some early mcu  projects like captain america the first  avenger which brought in over 370  million dollars  in other words just because jupiter's  legacy may be over on netflix that  doesn't mean it's not still the start of  something big  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

